-- title:
--   The slice class is closed under subtraction
-- statement:
--   A vector field $w:\mathbb R^3\to\mathbb R^3$ is in the slice class when it is $C^\infty$ and all components $w_i$, all first partial derivatives $\partial_jw_i$ and all pure second derivatives $\partial_j^2w_i$ are square integrable. If $u$ and $v$ are in the slice class, then so is
--   $$
--   x\mapsto u(x)-v(x).
--   $$
--
--   This is needed because uniqueness is proved by estimating the difference of two solutions.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/MathematicalPhysics/NavierStokes/BalancedTransport/EnergySlice.lean#L25-L41

